One decision the plan left open: the "not a letter or a digit" step uses Unicode-aware `\p{L}\p{N}` instead of the old `[^a-z0-9]`, so accented letters that survive as letters (e.g. `ø`, `ß`, Greek/Cyrillic) are kept rather than dashed — that's implied by the accented-letter support and leaves plain-ASCII behavior unchanged. Not merged, per instruction.

